            </profile>
            <profile id="eb09-c6e6-815e-d402" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Heavy troops are armed with hand weapon and light armour. Half the unit has bow and the other half sling (-1 point). Heavy Troops: Slingers in the second rank may shoot at full effect if the unit is stationary. Assyrian troops trained specially to fight in this way, which is an exception to the normal use of slings only by skirmishers. Cause Fear. Mounted Infantry: hand weapon, light armour and bow.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="7ab3-aed9-b13e-1859" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
